IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr2-helpers`

-- PART 4 -- RELIANCE AND RECORD-KEEPING (regulations 39 to 41) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of
-- Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692), United Kingdom.  Lines 1240-1319 of the text.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is
-- verified against the official text.
--
-- LAYER 1: THE LAW, OBJECTIVELY.  A rule answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (a MAYBE BOOLEAN):
-- JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING where it does not answer.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ANOTHER SECTION ANSWERS (seams, see NOTES.md "Seams (mlr2)"):
--   S-7, S-8   `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`                                              (regulation 8, part mlr1)
--   S-14       `reg 64C, 64D or 64G the relevant person holds information or documents received under that regulation` (regs 64C, 64D, 64G, part mlr3)

§ `Part 4 -- Reliance and record-keeping (regulations 39 to 41)`

§§ `Regulation 39 -- Reliance`

-- reg 39(3): the persons the relevant person may rely on.  Regulation 39(1) hands "a person who falls within paragraph (3)" to this list, so a person in none of the heads answers JUST FALSE (fork F39-1).  Sub-paragraph (b) is blank in this text.
-- SEAM S-7 (asking)
-- src:1248 | (3) The persons within this paragraph are—
-- src:1249 | (a) another relevant person who is subject to these Regulations under regulation 8;
-- src:1250 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1251 | (c) a person who carries on business in a third country who is—
-- src:1252 | (i) subject to requirements in relation to customer due diligence and record keeping which are equivalent to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive; and
-- src:1253 | (ii) supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive;
-- src:1254 | (d) organisations whose members consist of persons within sub-paragraph (a)... or (c).
@ref reg 39(3) (src:1248-1254)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person carries on business in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to requirements in relation to customer due diligence and record keeping which are equivalent to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an organisation whose members consist of persons within sub-paragraph (a) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(3) the person falls within paragraph (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        IF `the person carries on business in a third country`
           AND `the person is subject to requirements in relation to customer due diligence and record keeping which are equivalent to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive`
           AND `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
        IF `the person is an organisation whose members consist of persons within sub-paragraph (a) or (c)` THEN JUST TRUE -- (d)
        IF `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant person is regulation 8's answer and has not been given
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons within this paragraph are" -- regulation 39(1) hands reliance to the persons "who fall within paragraph (3)", a definition the text itself hands to a list, so a person in none of the heads is not within it (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated definitions (a); fork F39-1)

-- reg 39(1): the permission, and the liability that stays.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1242 | (1) A relevant person may rely on a person who falls within paragraph (3) (“the third party”) to apply any of the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10) , or to carry out any of the measures required by regulation 30A, but, notwithstanding the relevant person's reliance on the third party, the relevant person remains liable for any failure to apply such measures.
@ref reg 39(1) (src:1242-1242)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 39(3) the person falls within paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the measure is one required by regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10), or by regulation 30A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(1) the relevant person may rely on the third party` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `reg 39(3) the person falls within paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the measure is one required by regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10), or by regulation 30A`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of reliance "on a person who falls within paragraph (3)" to apply "the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10), or ... regulation 30A"; the paragraph says nothing of any other reliance

-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1242 | (1) A relevant person may rely on a person who falls within paragraph (3) (“the third party”) to apply any of the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10) , or to carry out any of the measures required by regulation 30A, but, notwithstanding the relevant person's reliance on the third party, the relevant person remains liable for any failure to apply such measures.
@ref reg 39(1) (src:1242-1242)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person relies on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(1) the relevant person remains liable for any failure to apply such measures` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person relies on the third party`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notwithstanding the relevant person's reliance on the third party, the relevant person remains liable"; the paragraph says nothing where there is no reliance

-- reg 39(2): "When a relevant person relies on the third party ..., it (a) must ...; (b) must ...".
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1243 | (2) When a relevant person relies on the third party to apply customer due diligence measures or carry out any of the measures required by regulation 30A under paragraph (1) it—
-- src:1244 | (a) must immediately obtain from the third party all the information needed to satisfy the requirements of regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10) and regulation 30A in relation to the customer, customer's beneficial owner, or any person acting on behalf of the customer;
-- src:1245 | (b) must enter into arrangements with the third party which—
-- src:1246 | (i) enable the relevant person to obtain from the third party immediately on request copies of any identification and verification data and any other relevant documentation on the identity of the customer, customer's beneficial owner, or any person acting on behalf of the customer;
-- src:1247 | (ii) require the third party to retain copies of the data and documents referred to in paragraph (i) for the period referred to in regulation 40.
@ref reg 39(2) (src:1243-1247)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person relies on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(2) the relevant person must obtain the information and enter into the arrangements` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person relies on the third party`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a relevant person relies on the third party" ("when" counts as "where": a condition that fails gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); the duty does not arise through this function)

-- A compliance check, in the reading of marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md: an undischarged "must" is a "no".
-- src:1243 | (2) When a relevant person relies on the third party to apply customer due diligence measures or carry out any of the measures required by regulation 30A under paragraph (1) it—
-- src:1244 | (a) must immediately obtain from the third party all the information needed to satisfy the requirements of regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10) and regulation 30A in relation to the customer, customer's beneficial owner, or any person acting on behalf of the customer;
-- src:1245 | (b) must enter into arrangements with the third party which—
-- src:1246 | (i) enable the relevant person to obtain from the third party immediately on request copies of any identification and verification data and any other relevant documentation on the identity of the customer, customer's beneficial owner, or any person acting on behalf of the customer;
-- src:1247 | (ii) require the third party to retain copies of the data and documents referred to in paragraph (i) for the period referred to in regulation 40.
@ref reg 39(2) (src:1243-1247)
GIVEN `the relevant person relies on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it immediately obtained from the third party all the information needed to satisfy the requirements of regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10) and regulation 30A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it entered into arrangements which enable it to obtain from the third party immediately on request copies of any identification and verification data and other relevant documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those arrangements require the third party to retain copies of the data and documents for the period referred to in regulation 40` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(2) the relevant person has met the requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the relevant person relies on the third party`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): there is no duty to check: the duty function above answers no where the relevant person does not rely on the third party, and this check asks only whether a duty that arose was discharged
        IF `it immediately obtained from the third party all the information needed to satisfy the requirements of regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10) and regulation 30A`
           AND `it entered into arrangements which enable it to obtain from the third party immediately on request copies of any identification and verification data and other relevant documentation`
           AND `those arrangements require the third party to retain copies of the data and documents for the period referred to in regulation 40`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it (a) must immediately obtain ... (b) must enter into arrangements with the third party which (i) ... (ii) ..." (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 39(5): the disapplication of paragraph (4).
-- src:1256 | (5) Paragraph (4) does not apply to a branch or majority owned subsidiary of an entity ... if all the following conditions are met—
-- src:1257 | (a) the entity is—
-- src:1258 | (i) a person who is subject to the requirements in these Regulations as a relevant person within the meaning of regulation 8 and who is supervised for compliance with them; or
-- src:1259 | (ii) subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive) and supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive;
-- src:1260 | (b) the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under—
-- src:1261 | (i) regulation 20 of these Regulations, or
-- src:1262 | (ii) requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive.
@ref reg 39(5) (src:1256-1262)
GIVEN `the third party is a branch or majority owned subsidiary of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a person subject to the requirements in these Regulations as a relevant person within the meaning of regulation 8 and supervised for compliance with them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity, and supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of that directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under regulation 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(5) paragraph (4) does not apply to the third party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the third party is a branch or majority owned subsidiary of the entity`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (5) is an exception to the flat negative of paragraph (4) ("may not rely"), made for "a branch or majority owned subsidiary of an entity" that meets the conditions; for a third party that is not one the exception is not made and paragraph (4) stands (fork F39-4)
        IF (`the entity is a person subject to the requirements in these Regulations as a relevant person within the meaning of regulation 8 and supervised for compliance with them`
            OR `the entity is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity, and supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of that directive`)
           AND (`the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under regulation 20`
                OR `the branch or subsidiary complies fully with procedures and policies established for the group under requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if all the following conditions are met" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 39(4): "may not rely on a third party established in a FATF call for action country".  The text defines "high-risk third country" by
-- pointing at regulation 33(3), and the paragraph itself uses "FATF call for action country" (finding 2 of NOTES.md).
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1255 | (4) A relevant person may not rely on a third party established in a FATF call for action country, and for these purposes “high-risk third country” has the meaning given in regulation 33(3).
@ref reg 39(4) (src:1255-1255)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third party is established in a FATF call for action country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 39(5) paragraph (4) does not apply to the third party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(4) the relevant person may rely on the third party established in a FATF call for action country` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (BRANCH
            IF (NOT `the third party is established in a FATF call for action country`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a third party established in a FATF call for action country"
            IF `reg 39(5) paragraph (4) does not apply to the third party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (5) says that paragraph (4) "does not apply" to this third party
            IF `reg 39(5) paragraph (4) does not apply to the third party` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person may not rely on a third party established in a FATF call for action country"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (5) disapplies paragraph (4) has not been answered

-- reg 39(6): deemed compliance.
-- src:1263 | (6) A relevant person is to be treated by a supervisory authority as having complied with the requirements of paragraph (2) if—
-- src:1264 | (a) the relevant person is relying on information provided by a third party which is a member of the same group as the relevant person;
-- src:1265 | (b) that group applies customer due diligence measures, rules on record keeping and programmes against money laundering and terrorist financing in accordance with these Regulations, the fourth money laundering directive or rules having equivalent effect; and
-- src:1266 | (c) the effective implementation of the requirements referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is supervised at group level by—
-- src:1267 | (i) an authority of an EEA state ... with responsibility for the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive; or
-- src:1268 | (ii) an equivalent authority of a third country.
@ref reg 39(6) (src:1263-1268)
GIVEN `the relevant person is relying on information provided by a third party which is a member of the same group as the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that group applies customer due diligence measures, rules on record keeping and programmes against money laundering and terrorist financing in accordance with these Regulations, the fourth money laundering directive or rules having equivalent effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effective implementation of those requirements is supervised at group level by an authority of an EEA state with responsibility for the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effective implementation of those requirements is supervised at group level by an equivalent authority of a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(6) the relevant person is to be treated by a supervisory authority as having complied with the requirements of paragraph (2)` MEANS
    IF `the relevant person is relying on information provided by a third party which is a member of the same group as the relevant person`
       AND `that group applies customer due diligence measures, rules on record keeping and programmes against money laundering and terrorist financing in accordance with these Regulations, the fourth money laundering directive or rules having equivalent effect`
       AND (`the effective implementation of those requirements is supervised at group level by an authority of an EEA state with responsibility for the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive`
            OR `the effective implementation of those requirements is supervised at group level by an equivalent authority of a third country`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be treated ... as having complied with the requirements of paragraph (2) if" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 39(7): agents and outsourcing service providers.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1269 | (7) Nothing in this regulation prevents a relevant person applying customer due diligence measures , or carrying out any of the measures required by regulation 30A, by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider provided that the arrangements between the relevant person and the agent or outsourcing service provider provide for the relevant person to remain liable for any failure to apply such measures.
@ref reg 39(7) (src:1269-1269)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person applies customer due diligence measures, or carries out measures required by regulation 30A, by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements between the relevant person and the agent or outsourcing service provider provide for the relevant person to remain liable for any failure to apply such measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(7) nothing in this regulation prevents the relevant person applying the measures by means of the agent or outsourcing service provider` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (BRANCH
            IF (NOT `the relevant person applies customer due diligence measures, or carries out measures required by regulation 30A, by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applying customer due diligence measures ... by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider"
            IF `the arrangements between the relevant person and the agent or outsourcing service provider provide for the relevant person to remain liable for any failure to apply such measures`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the arrangements ... provide for the relevant person to remain liable for any failure to apply such measures" (a failed proviso, marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 39(8)
-- src:1270 | (8) For the purposes of paragraph (7), an “outsourcing service provider” means a person who—
-- src:1271 | (a) performs a process, a service or an activity that would otherwise be undertaken by the relevant person, and
-- src:1272 | (b) is not an employee of the relevant person.
@ref reg 39(8) (src:1270-1272)
GIVEN `the person performs a process, a service or an activity that would otherwise be undertaken by the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 39(8) the person is an outsourcing service provider` MEANS
    IF `the person performs a process, a service or an activity that would otherwise be undertaken by the relevant person` AND (NOT `the person is an employee of the relevant person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an 'outsourcing service provider' means a person who"

§§ `Regulation 40 -- Record-keeping`

-- reg 40(2): the records.  The list is not closed ("The records are"), and sub-paragraphs (c) and (d) speak of two cases.
DECLARE `reg 40(2) record` IS ONE OF
    `reg 40(2)(a) a copy of documents and information obtained to satisfy the customer due diligence requirements`
    `reg 40(2)(b) sufficient supporting records in respect of a transaction`
    `reg 40(2)(c) documents and information received in an inter-cryptoasset business transfer`
    `reg 40(2)(d) documents and information received in an unhosted wallet transfer`
    `reg 40(2) another record`

-- SEAM S-8 (asking); SEAM S-14 (asking)
-- src:1275 | (2) The records are—
-- src:1276 | (a) a copy of any documents and information obtained by the relevant person to satisfy the customer due diligence requirements in regulations 28, 29 and 33 to 37 and the requirements of regulation 30A , and of regulations 64C and 64G(1);
-- src:1277 | (b) sufficient supporting records (consisting of the original documents or copies) in respect of a transaction (whether or not the transaction is an occasional transaction) which is the subject of customer due diligence measures or ongoing monitoring to enable the transaction to be reconstructed.
-- src:1278 | (c) in the case of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer, in addition to the records referred to in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b), any documents and information received by an intermediary cryptoasset business and the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary by virtue of the obligations under regulations 64C(1), (2) and (7), or received by them pursuant to a request under regulation 64D(2)(a) or 64E(2)(a); and
-- src:1279 | (d) in the case of an unhosted wallet transfer, in addition to the records referred to in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b), any documents and information received by a cryptoasset business pursuant to a request under regulation 64G(1).
@ref reg 40(2) (src:1275-1279)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      record IS A `reg 40(2) record`
      `the case is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 64C, 64D or 64G the relevant person holds information or documents received under that regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(2) the record is one that the relevant person must keep` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (CONSIDER record
         WHEN `reg 40(2)(a) a copy of documents and information obtained to satisfy the customer due diligence requirements` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "The records are (a) a copy of any documents and information obtained"
         WHEN `reg 40(2)(b) sufficient supporting records in respect of a transaction` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "(b) sufficient supporting records ... to enable the transaction to be reconstructed"
         WHEN `reg 40(2)(c) documents and information received in an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` THEN
             IF `the case is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` AND `reg 64C, 64D or 64G the relevant person holds information or documents received under that regulation`
             THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "(c) in the case of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer"
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer"
         WHEN `reg 40(2)(d) documents and information received in an unhosted wallet transfer` THEN
             IF `the case is an unhosted wallet transfer` AND `reg 64C, 64D or 64G the relevant person holds information or documents received under that regulation`
             THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "(d) in the case of an unhosted wallet transfer"
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an unhosted wallet transfer"
         WHEN `reg 40(2) another record` THEN NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The records are" lists them and does not say "only"

-- reg 40(3) and (4): the period.
DECLARE `reg 40(3) kind of record` IS ONE OF
    `reg 40(3)(a) a record relating to an occasional transaction`
    `reg 40(3)(b)(i) a record relating to a transaction which occurs as part of a business relationship`
    `reg 40(3)(b)(ii) a record relating to customer due diligence measures taken in connection with a business relationship`

-- The day the period of five years begins on is the day the relevant person knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the
-- transaction is complete (an occasional transaction) or that the business relationship has come to an end.  The last day of the
-- period is the day before the fifth anniversary of that day.  A MAYBE DATE: NOTHING means the day has not come.
-- src:1280 | (3) Subject to paragraph (4), the period is five years beginning on the date on which the relevant person knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe—
-- src:1281 | (a) that the transaction is complete, for records relating to an occasional transaction; or
-- src:1282 | (b) that the business relationship has come to an end for records relating to—
-- src:1283 | (i) any transaction which occurs as part of a business relationship, or
-- src:1284 | (ii) customer due diligence measures taken in connection with that relationship.
@ref reg 40(3) (src:1280-1284)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 40(3) the last day of the period of five years` MEANS (`add years` start 5) MINUS 1

-- SEAM S-8 (asking).  "must keep the records ... for at least the period": the question is asked on a day.
-- src:1274 | (1) Subject to paragraph (5), a relevant person must keep the records specified in paragraph (2) for at least the period specified in paragraph (3).
@ref reg 40(1) (src:1274-1274)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the relevant person knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the transaction is complete or that the business relationship has come to an end` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(1) the relevant person must still keep the records on the date asked` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (CONSIDER `the date on which the relevant person knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the transaction is complete or that the business relationship has come to an end`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period of five years has not begun, because the transaction is not known to be complete and the business relationship is not known to have ended
         WHEN JUST start THEN
             BRANCH
                 IF `the date asked` LESS THAN start
                 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the period of five years beginning on the date on which the relevant person knows"; a day before that date is outside the period the text fixes in its own words (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
                 IF `the date asked` AT MOST `reg 40(3) the last day of the period of five years` start
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 OTHERWISE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for at least the period specified in paragraph (3)" -- "five years beginning on the date" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); the other reading, that "at least" sets a floor and says nothing of later days, is in NOTES.md

-- reg 40(4): the ten-year ceiling on records of transactions that occur as part of a business relationship.
-- src:1285 | (4) A relevant person is not required to keep the records referred to in paragraph (3)(b)(i) for more than 10 years.
@ref reg 40(4) (src:1285-1285)
GIVEN kind IS A `reg 40(3) kind of record`
      start IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(4) the relevant person is required to keep the record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `reg 40(3)(b)(i) a record relating to a transaction which occurs as part of a business relationship`
           AND `the date asked` GREATER THAN (`add years` start 10) MINUS 1
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not required to keep the records referred to in paragraph (3)(b)(i) for more than 10 years"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of the records in paragraph (3)(b)(i), and only of a period of more than 10 years

-- reg 40(5): deletion of personal data once the period has expired.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1286 | (5) Once the period referred to in paragraph (3), or if applicable paragraph (4), has expired, the relevant person must delete any personal data obtained for the purposes of these Regulations unless—
-- src:1287 | (a) the relevant person is required to retain records containing personal data—
-- src:1288 | (i) by or under any enactment, or
-- src:1289 | (ii) for the purposes of any court proceedings;
-- src:1290 | (b) the data subject has given consent to the retention of that data; or
-- src:1291 | (c) the relevant person has reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings.
@ref reg 40(5) (src:1286-1291)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the period referred to in paragraph (3) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is required to retain records containing the personal data by or under any enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is required to retain records containing the personal data for the purposes of any court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject has given consent to the retention of that data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(5) the relevant person must delete the personal data obtained for the purposes of these Regulations` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (BRANCH
            IF (NOT `the period referred to in paragraph (3) has expired`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Once the period referred to in paragraph (3), or if applicable paragraph (4), has expired, the relevant person must delete" ("once" is read as "where": before the period expires the duty is not triggered; assumed, not ruled; fork FW-1)
            IF `the relevant person is required to retain records containing the personal data by or under any enactment`
               OR `the relevant person is required to retain records containing the personal data for the purposes of any court proceedings`
               OR `the data subject has given consent to the retention of that data`
               OR `the relevant person has reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must delete any personal data ... unless" one of (a) to (c) applies
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE)

-- reg 40(6)
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1292 | (6) A relevant person who is relied on by another person must keep the records specified in paragraph (2) for the period referred to in paragraph (3) or, if applicable, paragraph (4).
@ref reg 40(6) (src:1292-1292)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is relied on by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(6) the relevant person who is relied on must keep the records specified in paragraph (2)` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person is relied on by another person`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant person who is relied on by another person"

-- reg 40(7) and (8): what A must do for B, and when.
-- src:1293 | (7) A person referred to in regulation 39(3) (“A”) who is relied on by a relevant person (“B”) must, if requested by B within the period referred to in paragraph (3) or, if applicable, paragraph (4), immediately—
-- src:1294 | (a) make available to B any information about the customer, any person purporting to act on behalf of the customer and any beneficial owner of the customer, which A obtained when applying customer due diligence measures; and
-- src:1295 | (b) forward to B copies of any identification and verification data and other relevant documents on the identity of the customer, any person purporting to act on behalf of the customer and any beneficial owner of the customer, which A obtained when applying those measures.
@ref reg 40(7) (src:1293-1295)
-- src:1296 | (8) Paragraph (7) does not apply where a relevant person applies customer due diligence measures by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider (within the meaning of regulation 39(8)).
@ref reg 40(8) (src:1296-1296)
GIVEN `reg 39(3) the person falls within paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is relied on by a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the relevant person asked for the information and documents` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the period referred to in paragraph (3) or, if applicable, paragraph (4)` IS A DATE
      `the relevant person applies customer due diligence measures by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(7) the person relied on must make the information available and forward copies of the data and documents to the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person applies customer due diligence measures by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (7) does not apply where a relevant person applies customer due diligence measures by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider"
        IF (NOT (`reg 39(3) the person falls within paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person is relied on by a relevant person`))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person referred to in regulation 39(3) ('A') who is relied on by a relevant person ('B')"
        IF `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day` `the date on which the relevant person asked for the information and documents` `the last day of the period referred to in paragraph (3) or, if applicable, paragraph (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, if requested by B within the period" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md: no request, or a request after the period)

-- reg 40(9)(a), (b): the first two definitions.
-- src:1297 | (9) For the purposes of this regulation—
@ref reg 40(9) (src:1297-1297)
-- src:1298 | (a) B relies on A where B does so in accordance with regulation 39(1);
@ref reg 40(9)(a) (src:1298-1298)
GIVEN `B relies on A in accordance with regulation 39(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(9)(a) B relies on A` MEANS
    IF `B relies on A in accordance with regulation 39(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "B relies on A where B does so in accordance with regulation 39(1)"

-- src:1299 | (b) “copy” means a copy of the original document which would be admissible as evidence of the original document in court proceedings;
@ref reg 40(9)(b) (src:1299-1299)
GIVEN `it is a copy of the original document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that copy would be admissible as evidence of the original document in court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 40(9)(b) the thing is a copy` MEANS
    IF `it is a copy of the original document` AND `that copy would be admissible as evidence of the original document in court proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'copy' means a copy of the original document which would be admissible as evidence"

-- reg 40(9)(c) to (e): terms defined by pointing at another instrument or at regulation 64B.
DECLARE `reg 40(9) term` IS ONE OF
    `reg 40(9)(c) data subject`
    `reg 40(9)(d) personal data`
    `reg 40(9)(e) beneficiary`
    `reg 40(9)(e) cryptoasset business`
    `reg 40(9)(e) inter-cryptoasset business transfer`
    `reg 40(9)(e) intermediary cryptoasset business`
    `reg 40(9)(e) unhosted wallet transfer`

-- src:1300 | (c) “data subject” has the same meaning as in the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3 of that Act);
-- src:1301 | (d) “personal data” has the same meaning as in Parts 5 to 7 of that Act (see section 3(2) and (14) of that Act).
-- src:1302 | (e) “beneficiary”, “cryptoasset business”, “inter-cryptoasset business transfer”, “intermediary cryptoasset business” and “unhosted wallet transfer” have the meanings given by regulation 64B.
@ref reg 40(9)(c) to (e) (src:1300-1302)
GIVEN term IS A `reg 40(9) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 40(9) the meaning of the term is given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `reg 40(9)(c) data subject` THEN "section 3 of the Data Protection Act 2018"
    WHEN `reg 40(9)(d) personal data` THEN "section 3(2) and (14) of the Data Protection Act 2018, for the purposes of Parts 5 to 7 of that Act"
    WHEN `reg 40(9)(e) beneficiary` THEN "regulation 64B"
    WHEN `reg 40(9)(e) cryptoasset business` THEN "regulation 64B"
    WHEN `reg 40(9)(e) inter-cryptoasset business transfer` THEN "regulation 64B"
    WHEN `reg 40(9)(e) intermediary cryptoasset business` THEN "regulation 64B"
    WHEN `reg 40(9)(e) unhosted wallet transfer` THEN "regulation 64B"

§§ `Regulation 41 -- Data protection`

-- reg 41(1): "may only be processed for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing".
DECLARE `reg 41(1) purpose of processing` IS ONE OF
    `reg 41(1) preventing money laundering`
    `reg 41(1) preventing terrorist financing`
    `reg 41(1) preventing proliferation financing`
    `reg 41(1) another purpose`

-- src:1304 | (1) Any personal data obtained by relevant persons for the purposes of these Regulations may only be processed for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing.
@ref reg 41(1) (src:1304-1304)
GIVEN `the personal data was obtained by a relevant person for the purposes of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `reg 41(1) purpose of processing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 41(1) the personal data may be processed for the purpose` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the personal data was obtained by a relevant person for the purposes of these Regulations`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any personal data obtained by relevant persons for the purposes of these Regulations"
    ELSE CONSIDER purpose
         WHEN `reg 41(1) preventing money laundering` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 41(1) preventing terrorist financing` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 41(1) preventing proliferation financing` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 41(1) another purpose` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be processed for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing"

-- reg 41(3): other uses.
-- src:1306 | (3) No other use may be made of personal data referred to in paragraph (1), unless—
-- src:1307 | (a) use of the data is permitted by or under an enactment other than these Regulations or the UK GDPR; or
-- src:1308 | (b) the relevant person has obtained the consent of the data subject to the proposed use of the data.
@ref reg 41(3) (src:1306-1308)
GIVEN `the personal data is personal data referred to in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `use of the data is permitted by or under an enactment other than these Regulations or the UK GDPR` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has obtained the consent of the data subject to the proposed use of the data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 41(3) another use of the personal data may be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the personal data is personal data referred to in paragraph (1)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No other use may be made of personal data referred to in paragraph (1)"
        IF `use of the data is permitted by or under an enactment other than these Regulations or the UK GDPR` OR `the relevant person has obtained the consent of the data subject to the proposed use of the data`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No other use may be made of personal data ... unless" (a) or (b)

-- reg 41(6): the statement to a new customer, given before the relationship or transaction.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1311 | (6) Before establishing a business relationship or entering into an occasional transaction with a new customer, as well as providing the customer with the information required under Article 13 of the UK GDPR (information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject), relevant persons must provide the customer with a statement that any personal data received from the customer will be processed only—
-- src:1312 | (a) for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing, or
-- src:1313 | (b) as permitted under paragraph (3).
@ref reg 41(6) (src:1311-1313)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the customer is a new customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that any personal data received from the customer will be processed only for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing, or as permitted under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the statement was provided to the customer` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the business relationship was established or the occasional transaction was entered into` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 41(6) the relevant person has provided the customer with the statement before establishing the business relationship or entering into the occasional transaction` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (BRANCH
            IF (NOT `the customer is a new customer`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with a new customer"
            IF `the statement says that any personal data received from the customer will be processed only for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing, or as permitted under paragraph (3)`
               AND (NOT (`the date on which the statement was provided to the customer` EQUALS NOTHING))
               AND `mlr2 the event was before the day` `the date on which the statement was provided to the customer` `the date on which the business relationship was established or the occasional transaction was entered into` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before establishing a business relationship or entering into an occasional transaction with a new customer ... relevant persons must provide the customer with a statement" (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 41(7)
-- src:1314 | (7) In Article 6(1) of the UK GDPR (lawfulness of processing), the reference in point (e) to processing of personal data that is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest includes processing of personal data in accordance with these Regulations that is necessary for the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing.
@ref reg 41(7) (src:1314-1314)
GIVEN `the processing is in accordance with these Regulations and is necessary for the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 41(7) the processing is processing necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest, within point (e) of Article 6(1) of the UK GDPR` MEANS
    IF `the processing is in accordance with these Regulations and is necessary for the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference in point (e) ... includes processing of personal data in accordance with these Regulations"; "includes" leaves other processing open

-- reg 41(8): a signpost to the Data Protection Act 2018.
-- src:1315 | (8) In the case of sensitive processing of personal data for the purposes of the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing, section 10 of, and Schedule 1 to, the Data Protection Act 2018 make provision about when the processing meets a requirement in Article 9(2) or 10 of the UK GDPR for authorisation under the law of the United Kingdom (see, for example, paragraphs 10, 11 and 12 of that Schedule).
@ref reg 41(8) (src:1315-1315)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 41(8) the provision about when sensitive processing meets a requirement of Article 9(2) or 10 of the UK GDPR is made by` MEANS
    "section 10 of, and Schedule 1 to, the Data Protection Act 2018"

-- reg 41(9): "sensitive processing" and the borrowed terms.
-- src:1316 | (9) In this regulation—
-- src:1317 | “data subject” has the same meaning as in the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3 of that Act);
-- src:1318 | “personal data” and “processing” have the same meaning as in Parts 5 to 7 of that Act (see section 3(2), (4) and (14) of that Act);
-- src:1319 | “sensitive processing” means the processing of personal data described in Article 9(1) or 10 of the UK GDPR (special categories of personal data and personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences etc).
@ref reg 41(9) (src:1316-1319)
GIVEN `the processing is of personal data described in Article 9(1) or 10 of the UK GDPR` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 41(9) the processing is sensitive processing` MEANS
    IF `the processing is of personal data described in Article 9(1) or 10 of the UK GDPR`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'sensitive processing' means the processing of personal data described in Article 9(1) or 10 of the UK GDPR"

DECLARE `reg 41(9) term` IS ONE OF
    `reg 41(9) data subject`
    `reg 41(9) personal data`
    `reg 41(9) processing`

-- src:1316 | (9) In this regulation—
-- src:1317 | “data subject” has the same meaning as in the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3 of that Act);
-- src:1318 | “personal data” and “processing” have the same meaning as in Parts 5 to 7 of that Act (see section 3(2), (4) and (14) of that Act);
-- src:1319 | “sensitive processing” means the processing of personal data described in Article 9(1) or 10 of the UK GDPR (special categories of personal data and personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences etc).
@ref reg 41(9) (src:1316-1319)
GIVEN term IS A `reg 41(9) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 41(9) the meaning of the term is given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `reg 41(9) data subject` THEN "section 3 of the Data Protection Act 2018"
    WHEN `reg 41(9) personal data` THEN "section 3(2) and (14) of the Data Protection Act 2018, for the purposes of Parts 5 to 7 of that Act"
    WHEN `reg 41(9) processing` THEN "section 3(4) of the Data Protection Act 2018, for the purposes of Parts 5 to 7 of that Act"
